  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the role of civil society organizations in harm reduction in the Middle East and North Africa - World - Multicountry MENA HRA (01-Jan-2014-30-Jun-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The spread of HIV infection through injecting drug use (IDU) is an increasingly serious public health problem in all countries included in this grant agreement: Afghanistan, Bahrain, Egypt, Iran (Islamic Republic), Jordan, Lebanon, Libya, Morocco, Oman, Pakistan, Syrian Arab Republic, Tunisia, West Bank and Gaza. The Program aims to create a regional platform that specifically promotes regional co-operation and learning, and to support at the country level CSOs and other stakeholders in implementing the acquired technical, managerial and leadership skills, and in developing harm reduction activities. The overall public health goal of the Program is to prolong and improve the quality of life of injecting drug users in the Middle East and North Africa. The Program will organize advocacy and training workshops at the regional level, which will allow participants to network and learn from experiences of the countries which have successfully implemented multisectoral approach to harm reduction. It will also build capacity and enhance knowledge and skills of CSOs and other key stakeholders to ultimately increase availability, access and coverage of quality harm reduction services for drug users. Plus, it will result in models and pilot programs that can demonstrate feasibility and provide a platform for learning by doing.</narrative>
  </description>
